<title>CHILE: Chile Oct-Dec unemployment falls to 5.4 percent.</title>
<headline>Chile Oct-Dec unemployment falls to 5.4 percent.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's unemployment rate fell to 5.4 percent in the October-December quarter, down 0.5 percent from the previous quarter and 1.2 percent lower than in the same period of 1995, said the National Statistics Institute.  </p>
<p>The highest unemployment level was reported in the Eighth Region, with a jobless rate of 6.3 percent.  The lowest was in the southern Tenth Region, where unemployment was at 2.8 percent.</p>
<p>The unemployment rate in Santiago, where nearly half of Chile's population lives, was 6.2 percent.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
